       <name slugifiedName="name-updates-to-home-networking-control-protocol">Updates to Home Networking Control Protocol</name>
       <t indent="0" pn="section-5-1">The final paragraph in <xref target="RFC7788" section="8" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7788#section-8" derivedContent="RFC7788"/>, the Home Networking
 Control Protocol, is updated as follows:</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-2">OLD:
-   Names and unqualified zones are used in an HNCP network to provide
-   naming and service discovery with local significance.  A network-
-   wide zone is appended to all single labels or unqualified zones in
-   order to qualify them. &quot;.home&quot; is the default; however, an
-   administrator <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> configure the announcement of a Domain-Name TLV
-   (Section 10.6) for the network to use a different one.  In case
-   multiple are announced, the domain of the node with the greatest
-   node identifier takes precedence.</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-3">NEW:
-   Names and unqualified zones are used in an HNCP network to provide
-   naming and service discovery with local significance.  A network-
-   wide zone is appended to all single labels or unqualified zones in
-   order to qualify them. 'home.arpa.' is the default; however, an
-   administrator <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> configure the announcement of a Domain-Name TLV
-   (Section 10.6) for the network to use a different one.  In case
-   multiple TLVs are announced, the domain of the node with the
-   greatest node identifier takes precedence.</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-4"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   The 'home.arpa.' special-use name does not require a special
-   resolution protocol.  Names for which the rightmost two labels are
-   'home.arpa.' are resolved using the DNS protocol [RFC1035].
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-2">OLD:</t>
+      <blockquote pn="section-5-3">
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-5-3.1">Names and unqualified zones are used in an HNCP network to provide
+naming and service discovery with local significance.  A network-wide
+zone is appended to all single labels or unqualified zones in
+order to qualify them. &quot;.home&quot; is the default; however, an
+administrator <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> configure the announcement of a Domain-Name TLV
+(Section 10.6) for the network to use a different one.  In case
+multiple are announced, the domain of the node with the greatest
+node identifier takes precedence.</t>
+      </blockquote>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-4">NEW:</t>
+      <blockquote pn="section-5-5">
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-5-5.1">Names and unqualified zones are used in an HNCP network to provide
+naming and service discovery with local significance.  A network-wide
+zone is appended to all single labels or unqualified zones in
+order to qualify them. 'home.arpa.' is the default; however, an
+administrator <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> configure the announcement of a Domain-Name TLV
+(Section 10.6) for the network to use a different one.  In case
+multiple TLVs are announced, the domain of the node with the
+greatest node identifier takes precedence.</t>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-5-5.2">The 'home.arpa.' special-use name does not require a special
+resolution protocol.  Names for which the rightmost two labels are
+'home.arpa.' are resolved using the DNS protocol <xref target="RFC1035" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1035"/>.</t>
+      </blockquote>
